# su Command (Switch User)

`su` means **switch user**.

It is used to log in as another user inside the terminal.

---

## Basic Usage

```bash
su username

Examples:
su user
su or su root


# sudo Command (Superuser Do)

`sudo` allows a normal user to run commands as **root (administrator)**.

It is used when you need administrative permissions.

---

## Basic Usage

```bash
sudo command
